        "content": {
          "header": "",
          "subheader": "",
          "headerLayout": 0,
          "headerPosition": "",
          "headerLink": "",
          "type": "mask_imgtext",
          "title": "Leiba",
          "text": "<p>For millions of years, nature has shaped all life as it exists today on the mountain. In the Alps, humans have adapted to the sudden changes of wind and weather and the challenges that each season brings. Living on the mountain requires skill and the use of all the senses: collecting wood from the surrounding forests and preparing it for the winter, clearing the house and farm from drifts after stormy snowfalls, working with stone, wood and other materials from the mountains. Collecting water directly from the mountain spring and feeling it on your skin. These are activities that become anchored in one’s memory because they ensure survival on the mountain by working together.&nbsp;</p>",
